  "narrative": "The 12 new results are formal context-interaction tests for the five major accepted dataset-specific associations, plus one TMED10 specificity probe. I read signed interaction estimates as follows: a positive value means the exposed-minus-comparator contrast is larger, or more consistent with the claimed main-effect direction, in the named subgroup than in its aggregate complement; a negative value means the opposite. These are interaction contrasts, not direct mean differences, and the complements may contain heterogeneous culture/library/batch contexts, so I do not interpret them as causal context effects.\n\nFor the largest effects, lineage-subtype and culture interactions are mostly very small. H102 SMARCA4-loss x adenocarcinoma for SMARCA2 is -0.028 (95% CI -0.076 to +0.020), tiny relative to the main SMARCA2 association around +0.78 to +0.80; I reject this as evidence of meaningful adenocarcinoma-specific modification. H103 KEAP1-loss x adenocarcinoma for NFE2L2 is -0.012 (CI -0.057 to +0.033), also negligible relative to the NFE2L2 main effect around +0.80; reject. H104 MSI-high x adenocarcinoma for WRN is -0.021 (CI -0.085 to +0.042). The point is near zero, but the lower bound reaches about 10% of the main WRN effect and the non-adenocarcinoma complement is smaller, so I leave it unresolved rather than declaring a precise null. H105 TP53-loss x adenocarcinoma for USP7 is -0.038 (CI -0.190 to +0.115); this is near null in point estimate but too imprecise to exclude meaningful modification, so unresolved and deferred.\n\nFor culture context, H106 SMARCA4-loss x adherent for SMARCA2 is +0.015 (CI -0.029 to +0.058), far too small relative to the huge main SMARCA2 effect; reject. H107 KEAP1-loss x adherent for NFE2L2 is -0.019 (CI -0.064 to +0.027), small relative to the main NFE2L2 effect; reject. H108 MSI-high x adherent for WRN is the main signal: +0.105 (CI +0.037 to +0.172), statistically nonzero and suggesting that the MSI-high effect is larger in adherent culture than in the aggregate non-adherent complement. However, the lower bound corresponds to only a few percent of the main WRN effect, the non-adherent MSI-high exposed cell is only n=29, and this is one of many multiplicity-tested interactions. I therefore do not accept it as a clinically meaningful or stable interaction yet; I request independent validation of H108.\n\nFor the moderate STAT3 and USP7 associations, formal interactions are not precise enough to establish or exclude meaningful effect modification. H109 PTEN-loss x adherent for STAT3 is -0.023 (CI -0.149 to +0.104); H110 TP53-loss x adherent for USP7 is +0.080 (CI -0.094 to +0.254); H111 PTEN-loss x high screen quality for STAT3 is -0.027 (CI -0.131 to +0.076); H112 TP53-loss x high screen quality for USP7 is +0.066 (CI -0.078 to +0.209). All intervals cross zero and are wide relative to the main effects, so I leave them unresolved and deferred. Their near-zero point estimates make strong context modification less likely, but they do not rule out moderate modification.\n\nH115 tests whether SMARCA4 loss produces a generic dependency-score shift by examining dependency_TMED10. The estimate is -0.005 (CI -0.025 to +0.014), practically null. I reject the hypothesized SMARCA4-loss association with stronger TMED10 dependency. This supports specificity of the SMARCA4-loss association for SMARCA2 rather than a broad artifact across at least this unrelated dependency score. Overall, the new evidence strengthens context stability for the major SMARCA2 and NFE2L2 associations, leaves the WRN lineage and adherent-culture interactions somewhat open, and shows that the STAT3 and USP7 interaction tests are underpowered or imprecise. All conclusions remain dataset-specific associations, not causal or generalizable claims.",
  "research_notes": "Round 8 appraise update. Formal interaction tests: reject meaningful lineage interactions for SMARCA4/SMARCA2 (H102) and KEAP1/NFE2L2 (H103); reject adherent-culture interactions for SMARCA4/SMARCA2 (H106) and KEAP1/NFE2L2 (H107). H115 rejects a SMARCA4-loss association with TMED10 dependency, supporting specificity of SMARCA4 loss for SMARCA2 rather than a generic dependency shift. H104 MSI-high x adenocarcinoma for WRN remains unresolved because the lower CI reaches ~10% of the main effect and cells are imbalanced. H105 lineage interaction for TP53/USP7 remains unresolved and imprecise. H108 MSI-high x adherent for WRN is positive and statistically nonzero (+0.105, CI +0.037 to +0.172), suggesting larger MSI-high effect in adherent cultures, but the lower bound is modest, the non-adherent MSI-high exposed n=29, and multiplicity is high; validation requested. H109-H112 interactions for STAT3/USP7 remain unresolved and deferred; points are near zero but CIs allow moderate effect modification. Next priorities: await H108 validation; consider running screen-quality interactions for SMARCA2/NFE2L2/WRN if useful; keep QC=0 direct subsets H113/H114, TMED10 serum H116, and marker-F probe H117 low priority unless needed for specificity. Current main accepted associations remain SMARCA4 loss with stronger SMARCA2 dependency, KEAP1 loss with weaker NFE2L2 dependency, MSI-high with stronger WRN dependency, PTEN loss with stronger STAT3 dependency, and TP53 loss with weaker USP7 dependency, all dataset-specific and noncausal.",
