  "narrative": "All estimates are already signed to the registered hypothesis direction. The QC-incomplete robustness probes remained large and precise: PTEN loss is associated with lower dependency_STAT3 by +0.217 (95% CI +0.105 to +0.329) among matched-QC-incomplete lines, and TP53 loss with higher, i.e. weaker, dependency_USP7 by +0.428 (95% CI +0.271 to +0.586); accept and close because the lower bounds exceed the 10% absolute-dependency benchmark by a wide margin. H134 remains unresolved: complete-QC KRAS-mutant lines show only +0.016 (95% CI -0.003 to +0.036) for dependency_KRAS, smaller than a canonical effect would be and below the 10% point benchmark, although the upper bound is borderline; because several KRAS probes are weak and validation would be imprecise for a small effect, I defer it rather than request validation. The specificity probes are unsupported: KRAS mutation for BRAF dependency in the registered positive direction is actually negative and null (H131 -0.016, CI -0.034 to +0.001); ERBB2 amplification for EGFR dependency is near null (H133 +0.003, CI -0.023 to +0.030); and ERBB2 amplification for ERBB2 dependency among EGFR-amplification-negative lines is essentially zero (H135 +0.001, CI -0.028 to +0.030); reject and close these as unsupported in this dataset. The mutation-burden and Avana-library strata show that the large accepted associations persist: TP53 loss versus intact for dependency_USP7 is +0.546 (CI +0.422 to +0.670) in high mutation burden; KEAP1 loss versus intact for dependency_NFE2L2 is +0.795 (CI +0.771 to +0.818) in lower/moderate mutation burden; MSI-high for dependency_WRN is +0.800 (CI +0.745 to +0.854) in lower/moderate mutation burden; PTEN loss for dependency_STAT3 is +0.276 (CI +0.181 to +0.371) in high mutation burden; SMARCA4 loss for dependency_SMARCA2 is +0.781 (CI +0.760 to +0.802) and KEAP1 loss for dependency_NFE2L2 is +0.796 (CI +0.774 to +0.818) in the Avana library. All lower bounds are far above the clinical-significance threshold, so accept and close. These subset tests reduce concern that the main effects are proxies for mutation burden or library-specific artifacts, but they remain dataset-specific associations and do not establish causality or external generalizability. I request no validation now because the newly accepted results are already large and robust, and the only borderline canonical effect, H134, is small enough that validation is unlikely to support a clinically meaningful KRAS-dependency gain.",
  "research_notes": "Round 10 appraisal: accepted H113, H114, H138-H143 as robustness or specificity-persistence results; rejected H131, H133, H135 as cross-driver or null probes; kept H134 unresolved and deferred because KRAS mutation effect on dependency_KRAS is small, imprecise, and below the clinical benchmark. No validation requested. Active unanalyzed claims remain H116, H117, H130, H132, H136, H137. Durable robust associations are SMARCA4 loss with much stronger SMARCA2 dependency, KEAP1 loss with weaker NFE2L2 dependency, MSI-high with much stronger WRN dependency, PTEN loss with stronger STAT3 dependency, and TP53 loss with weaker USP7 dependency, supported across QC, screen-quality, mutation-burden, library, batch, and culture subsets with negligible screen-quality interactions. Remaining uncertainty includes small canonical KRAS mutation effects, ERBB2 amplification nulls, MDM2/TP53 nulls, and unanalyzed media/marker probes. Next analyze active unanalyzed probes and reserve validation unless a new high-value borderline or strong effect emerges."
